YAML STRUCTURE:
The workflow MUST follow this exact structural pattern:

name: CI
on:
  push:
    branches:
    - {{ analysis.default_branch }}
  pull_request:
    branches:
    - {{ analysis.default_branch }}
permissions:
  contents: read
concurrency:
  group: {% raw %}${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}{% endraw %}
  cancel-in-progress: true
jobs:
  <job definitions here>

JOB ORGANIZATION:
{% if analysis.build_command and analysis.test_command %}
Use TWO jobs:
  1. A "build" job containing applicable setup, cache, install, and build steps listed below.
{% if analysis.publish_dir or analysis.build_command %}
     At the END of the build job, upload compiled build output artifacts using `actions/upload-artifact@v4`
     (name: 'build-output', path: '{{ analysis.publish_dir or "dist" }}'). NEVER publish the workspace root (`.`).
{% endif %}
  2. A "test" job (needs: build) containing applicable setup, cache, install, test, and upload steps listed below.
{% if analysis.publish_dir or analysis.build_command %}
     At the START of the test job (after setup/cache/install), download the build artifact using
     `actions/download-artifact@v4` (name: 'build-output', path: '{{ analysis.publish_dir or "dist" }}') BEFORE running any test command.
     Only use `--no-build` or equivalent skip-build flags when this download step is present.
{% endif %}
  IMPORTANT: Jobs in GitHub Actions do NOT share a filesystem. If the build job uploads artifacts and the test job downloads them, `--no-build` flags can be used safely.
{% elif analysis.build_command %}
Use a SINGLE "build" job containing applicable setup, cache, install, and build steps listed below. Do NOT include test steps.
{% if analysis.publish_dir or analysis.build_command %}
At the END of the build job, upload compiled build output artifacts using `actions/upload-artifact@v4`
(name: 'build-output', path: '{{ analysis.publish_dir or "dist" }}'). NEVER publish the workspace root (`.`).
{% endif %}
{% elif analysis.test_command %}
Use a SINGLE "test" job containing applicable setup, cache, install, test, and upload steps listed below.
{% else %}
There are NO build steps and NO test steps. Omit the CI jobs entirely and generate ONLY the "docker" job. Do NOT generate a dummy CI job or dummy install steps.
{% endif %}
{% if analysis.environment_requirements %}

